Feature: EN 1992 structural scene
  The pure projection of the reinforced-concrete snapshot and its check report to a locale-free structural scene, its diagrams and its drag handles.
  The numbers come from the stdlib-only Python oracle in the oracles folder.

  Further specification assertions, asserted by the Rust unit tests of the crate and not by the platform adapters:
  - every fixture projects to a valid scene: Given the EN 1992 fixtures "compliant office frame", "failing under-reinforced", "compliant prestressed beam", "failing prestressed beam" and "liquid-retaining tank" When each fixture is projected with the report of its check engine Then the scene, every diagram and every handle validates with unique ids and English and German accessible names
  - a beam is drawn with its real reinforcement: Given the member "beam-B1" with 4 bars of 20 mm, 8 mm links at 150 mm and 35 mm cover When the scene is projected Then there is one rebar entity per bar and one link cage with floor((span - 2 cover) / spacing) + 1 links And the cover shell, two supports, the load glyphs and the deflected-shape overlay exist
  - the bending resistance of the capacity surface equals the closed form: Given the member "beam-B1" in C30/37 with B500B When the neutral axis is searched for N = 0 with the compression face on top Then MRd equals 214958.646 Nm within a relative 1e-6 And the crack spacing sr,max equals 0.2197 m and the simply supported deflection equals 3.289 mm
  - the 500 degC isotherm of a bottom-heated slab follows the implicit 1D oracle: Given the standard fire duration of <minutes> minutes on a 0.4 m slab heated from below Then the isotherm depth of the 2D transient conduction solve equals <depth> m within 2.5e-3 m And the oracle's own solver reproduces the closed-form erfc solution of constant properties within 0.1 K Examples (4 rows: 30-0-010493288942393745, 60-0-022213696885220634, 90-0-031058201417511318, 120-0-038539786363084694)
  - handles write the bound fields: Given a projected scene Then every handle is attached to an entity, its bindings resolve to a field path, and the drag parameter 0 reproduces the current field value
  - check stations colour the members, the cracks and the deflected shape: Given the report of the check engine with 11 stations on the flexure, shear, crack width and deflection checks When the scene is projected Then the concrete binding carries the envelope of those stations, the crack triangles are drawn only where the crack-width station is positive with their station width, and the deflected shape samples the deflection stations
  - creep coefficient and shrinkage strain over the concrete age follow Annex B: Given a C30/37 member of 0.30 m x 0.50 m at 50 % relative humidity, loaded at 28 days with normal-hardening cement When the concrete age track is sampled at <days> days Then the creep coefficient equals <phi> and the total shrinkage strain equals <eps> within 1e-9 relative Examples (2 rows: 365-1-8050930455938727-0-000375264706058797, 18250-2-369266541894601-0-00046660233312044463)
  - The shear truss, the strut-and-tie model and the critical shear sections agree with the checks crate: Given a committed beam with links and a shear check When the structural scene and its diagrams are projected Then the link resistance V_Rd,s is linear in cot theta and the strut resistance V_Rd,max falls with it And the strut-and-tie forces close the equilibrium of the load node and the support node And a translucent shear plane stands at the distance d from each support, coloured by the shear utilisation
  - the grade diagrams are the catalogue entries M-02, M-08 and the Annex C table: Given a C30/37 grade and a B500B grade When the diagrams "concrete-properties", "steel-law" and "ductility-class" are projected Then f_cm equals f_ck + 8 = 38 MPa, the inclined branch ends at k f_yd at 0.9 eps_uk, the grade point lies in the class region of Table C.1 and a k below the class minimum turns the point to the error tone
  - the bond diagrams and the anchorage and lap zones agree with B-01, B-02 and the member checks: Given a beam with a bar layer of 20 mm in good bond When the diagrams "bond-strength" and "anchorage-length" and the zones are projected Then the markers equal f_bd and l_b,rqd of the report, the zone length equals the limit of the anchorage check and a thicker bar lengthens it
  - the tying system case draws the ties of EN 1992-1-1 9.10: Given a DT-14 case with the span 6 m Then four peripheral, three internal and four column or wall tie entities stand on the slab, the tie of the case is drawn full and the others ghosted, and the diagram "tying-forces" marker equals the utilisation of the check and drags the span
  - the prestress limit diagram agrees with A-16: Given a prestressed beam When the diagram "prestress-limit" is projected Then the marker utilisation equals that of the check and its height over the limit equals the utilisation
  - the integrity matrix marks dangling references: Given a member whose reinforcement grade id is not declared Then the diagram "integrity" shows one error marker and the member carries an integrity label
